      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`BlockManager` currently invokes `fatalError` and `flushError` callbacks synchronously during storage operations, making it unsafe to protect those operations with a non-recursive mutex.\r\n\r\nThis PR introduces `BlockStorageOutcome<T>` to return the operation result together with ordered notifications. Callers dispatch them after the storage operation returns, including when a successful rollover produces multiple flush errors.\r\n\r\nAlso remove the notification dependency from `BlockManager` and add coverage for ordered flush errors and fatal errors.",
